        "abstract": "This paper presents a course model for teaching component-based software development (CBSD) in the software engineering undergraduate curriculum to deepen and broaden student comprehension of component software. All hands-on lab practices are designed with open-source software tools. The course endows students the precious experiences of making design decisions via comparative study, risk analysis, and synthesis of a vast number of open-source components.",
